@startuml seq_sel_invalid_position
title SC-SEL-02 - Invalid selector position

actor "Console user" as User
participant "Console" as Console
participant "Plant model" as Plant
participant "TCU" as TCU
participant "Red LED\n(TCU board)" as LED

note over User, LED
Covers: SYS-SEL-002, SYS-FLT-002, SYS-FLT-003, SYS-FLT-004, SYS-FLT-008, SYS-FLT-001, SYS-HMI-001, SIM-CON-003, SG-03
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

User -> Console : inject an invalid selector value (SIM-CON-003)
Console -> Plant : selector fault injection
Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector = 4 .. 7 (invalid) (t0, first invalid frame)
loop every 10 ms
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector invalid
end
... invalid for longer than 100 ms ...

alt last valid position before the fault was P, R or N
  TCU -> TCU : t0 + 100 ms: treat the selector as N, set the selector fault\n(FaultBits 0, DTC P0705-29) (SYS-SEL-002)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: solenoid pattern of SYS-SEL-005, SLS = OFF, RLS = OFF, FaultLamp = OFF
  note right of TCU: not a limp-home condition (SYS-FLT-002);\nno requirement of system_requirements\nsection 3.5 asks for the lamp (SYS-HMI-001)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: Mode = 0 (Normal), FaultBits bit 0 = 1
  Plant -> Plant : no drive (treated as N): safe state of SG-03
  User -> Console : remove the injection
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector valid (t2)
  ... valid position received for 500 ms ...
  TCU -> TCU : t2 + 500 ms: selector fault cleared (SYS-SEL-002, SYS-FLT-008)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: FaultBits bit 0 = 0
else last valid position before the fault was D
  TCU -> TCU : t0 + 100 ms: treat the selector as N, set the selector fault\n(SYS-SEL-002) -> enter limp-home, latched (SYS-FLT-002, SYS-FLT-004)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = OFF, PCS_Duty = 0 %, FaultLamp = ON,\nSLS = OFF, RLS = OFF (SYS-FLT-001)
  note right of TCU: <= 100 ms after the fault is set (SYS-FLT-003)
  TCU -> LED : ON (SYS-HMI-001)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: Mode = 1 (Limp-home), FaultBits bit 0 = 1
  User -> Console : remove the injection
  Plant -> TCU : SIM_Driver: Selector valid (t2)
  ... valid position received for 500 ms ...
  TCU -> TCU : t2 + 500 ms: selector fault cleared (SYS-SEL-002, SYS-FLT-008);\nlimp-home stays latched until the next power cycle (SYS-FLT-004)
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Actuators: SS_A = OFF, SS_B = OFF, PCS_Duty = 0 %, FaultLamp = ON
  TCU -> Plant : TCU_Status: Mode = 1 (Limp-home), FaultBits bit 0 = 0
end

note over Plant, TCU: Safe state of SG-03: an unknown position is treated as N, no drive torque is prepared.
@enduml
